# Cursor Rules for angband3d

Before starting work, review `AGENTS.md` and `docs/LLM_CONTEXT.md`.

## Key Commands
- Build C Engine: `$env:MSYSTEM='MINGW64'; $env:CHERE_INVOKING='1'; & C:\msys64\usr\bin\bash.exe -lc "cd /c/Dev/angband3d/engine && cmake --build build"`
- Build Godot C#: `dotnet build client/angband3d.csproj`
- Run Smoke Tests: `python tools/smoke_test.py`
- Play Game: `.\play.cmd`

## Context & Token Efficiency
- Do not perform recursive repository searches for standard classes; use the File Map in `AGENTS.md`.
- Prefer minimal surgical edits with `replace_string_in_file` / `multi_replace_string_in_file`.
- Check `docs/NEXT_STEPS.md` to immediately resume tasks without repeating research.

## Core Invariants
- Engine changes stay in `engine/src/main-bridge.c` and `engine/src/bridge-json.c`.
- Export patch: `cd engine; git diff 4.2.6..HEAD --output=..\engine-patch\0001-bridge-frontend.patch` (never use `>`).
- Always check `bridge_in_play()` before accessing `cave` or `player->grid`.
- Use `bridge_get_equipped_by_type()` rather than `slot_by_name()`.
- Movement = arrow keys. Turning = camera yaw only (0 game turns).
- View routing = `NeedsTerminal(frame)` in `Main.cs`.
